<title>BAHRAIN: Saudi 52-week T-bill rate falls to 5.8427 percent.</title>
<headline>Saudi 52-week T-bill rate falls to 5.8427 percent.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The yield on 52-week Saudi treasury bills worth 500 million riyals fell to 5.8427 percent from 6.0860 percent last month, a banker said.</p>
<p>The average price was 94.42188 from 94.20313 last month.</p>
<p>The bills are offered once a month by the Saudi Arabian Monetary Agency to Saudi-based banks.</p>
<p>One-year Saudi riyal interbank deposit rates were quoted at 5-15/16, 13/16.</p>
</text>
